        <item>
            <title>0.25.8</title>
            <pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:27:16 -0500</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>55</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.25.8</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>:root{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.45 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,system-ui,sans-serif;color:#1d1d1f;margin:0;padding:2px 4px}h3{font-size:13px;font-weight:600;margin:0 0 6px}ul{margin:0;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 4px}code{font:12px ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){body{color:#f5f5f7}}</style><h3>What's new in Keeploop 0.25.8</h3><ul><li>Monitors can now skip mail: Not from, Subject doesn't have and Message doesn't have each take a comma-separated list, and mail matching any of them never triggers the monitor.</li><li>AI apps now set monitors with one clear tool per kind: email, texts and WhatsApp, calls, notifications, Notes, Slack and calendar. Web and phone apps see the kinds you allow in Remote access.</li><li>Clicking a monitor's notification now opens that monitor in Settings &gt; Monitors.</li><li>Approval windows now name the AI app that is asking and show its icon.</li><li>AI apps now get accurate answers about what they may do: explaining a permission gives the same decision Keeploop makes when the app acts.</li><li>Setup steps now call the connector Keeploop. It is named Keeploop Remote only in Claude and ChatGPT.</li></ul>]]></description>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
